# React 19 Modern Architecture Rules

## Core Standards
- Use the modern React 19 hooks (`useActionState`, `useOptimistic`, `useFormStatus`, `use()`) instead of manual loading and error state management.
- Prefer passing Promises to `<Suspense>` boundaries using `use(promise)` inside Server-Rendered children.
- Never wrap components in `memo()` or `useCallback()` unless profiling proves performance bottlenecks; React 19 Compiler handles automatic memoization.
- For optimistic UI updates, always provide a clean rollback mechanism when action execution fails.
